cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this atlas, please cite it as below."
title: "A harmonized human glioblastoma chromatin accessibility atlas (snATAC-seq, 48 patients, 8 cohorts, 1.52M nuclei)"
version: "2026-10-11"
date-released: "2026-10-11"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23252324"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.23252324"
    description: "Zenodo deposit of the atlas data artifacts (peak reference, pseudobulk matrix, per-report scores, polished reports)."
abstract: >-
  Harmonized snATAC-seq / snMultiome atlas across 8 published GBM cohorts
  (48 patients with ≥50 cells per label group, 1.52M nuclei, 1,958,753 union
  peaks, 74% de-novo vs CATLAS), scored per cell type with patient-level
  replication, cohort batch sanity, per-non-target-cell-type contamination for
  AAV safety, and arm-adjusted Daigle Z for CNV correction. Deliverables include
  top-100 polished per-report CSVs, a sortable combined HTML, and 16 per-report
  parquet score tables.
